-- title:
--   Place compatibility of the ℚ̄- and ℚ-level Igusa chart models
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell\nmid N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` for the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $N$, and $\overline{F}=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` for its Laurent base change inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. Assume $j_{\overline{F}}=$ `jBar N` (the coefficientwise image of $j$) is transcendental over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and non-zero, with $\overline{F}$ finite over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(j_{\overline{F}})$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(j_{\overline{F}}^{-1})$, and likewise for $j_F=$ `jFull N` over $\mathbb{Q}$. Assume given $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra isomorphisms $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` $\cong$ `chartRing` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\{j_{\overline{F}}\}$ (the elements of $\overline{F}$ integral over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[j_{\overline{F}}]$) and its analogue at $j_{\overline{F}}^{-1}$, each sending $1\otimes b$ to the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of $b$; and $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra isomorphisms $\mathbb{Q}\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}}$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` $\cong$ `chartRing` $\mathbb{Q}\,\{j_F\}$ and its analogue at $j_F^{-1}$, each sending $1\otimes b$ to $b$. Let $M_\eta=$ `CurveModel.ofGenerator` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\ j_{\overline{F}}$ and $M_0=$ `CurveModel.ofGenerator` $\mathbb{Q}\ j_F$ be the resulting two-chart smooth proper models, and let $e_\eta$, $e_0$ be isomorphisms from $M_\eta.C$, $M_0.C$ to the base changes of the Igusa scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) along $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, resp. $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}\to\mathbb{Q}$, each commuting with the structure morphisms to the base and each pinned on the two charts: the composite of $\iota_0$ (resp. $\iota_\infty$) with $e$ and the first projection is the spectrum of the corresponding chart-ring isomorphism composed with `includeRight`, followed by `ιFin` (resp. `ιInf`). The conclusion: for every $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $x$ of $M_\eta.C$ over the base, every morphism $y$ from $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to the $\mathbb{Q}$-base change of the Igusa scheme, and every closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$, if $y$ and $x\circ e_\eta$ have the same image in the Igusa scheme under the first projection, and if $e_0^{-1}\circ y$ carries the closed point of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $x_0$, then the preimage in $F$ of the valuation subring of the place of $\overline{F}$ attached to $x$ by `pointEquivPlace`, along $F\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\overline{F}$ ($b\mapsto 1\otimes b$ followed by `baseChangeEquiv`), equals the valuation subring of $M_0$`.placeOfPoint` $x_0$.
--
--   This is the place-compatibility clause relating the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-level and $\mathbb{Q}$-level two-chart models of the modular function field of level $N$ through generic-fibre identifications with the Igusa model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$: a valuation of $\overline{F}$ coming from a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point restricts on $F$ to the place given by the closed point of the $\mathbb{Q}$-model below it. It feeds the existence statement [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_genericFibreIso_chartPin_galoisCompat_and_ratPlaceCompat`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_genericFibreIso_chartPin_galoisCompat_and_ratPlaceCompat), which packages the chart-pinned generic-fibre isomorphism together with its Galois- and place-compatibility properties.
